  "name": null,
  "problem": "| **Age ($x$)** | **$3$** | **$5$** | **$7$** | **$9$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Height ($y$)** | $95$ | $106$ | $115$ | $125$ |\n\nThe table above gives the ages, in years, and the corresponding heights, in centimeters, of four children. The corresponding linear regression line fitted using this sample is $\\overset{^}{\\,y}=80.6+5x.$\nAssuming that all conditions for the simple regression model are satisfied, $\\overset{―}{x}=6,$ and $\\text{MSE}=0.35,$ find a $95%$ confidence interval for the slope of the regression line.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T>4.303)=0.025,$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $2$ degrees of freedom. Also, the standard error for the slope is given by* \n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\text{MSE}}{{S}_{xx}}}.\n$$",
